-- title:
--   Rigid-chart rotation order equals place width at q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime subject to $hq2 : q = 2$, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ ($hqM'$).
--
--   **Guard prime.** A prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$.
--
--   **Valuation ring and supersingular place.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa, M')$ over $\kappa := \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, where $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa,M') = \kappa(\,j\text{-}q\text{-expansion},\ j(\mathsf q^{M'})\,)$ inside $\kappa((\mathsf q))$; the hypothesis $hW$ says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places in the sense of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, namely those places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa \to$ residue field of $w$ is onto), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\kappa$, i.e. every elliptic curve over $\kappa$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$. The hypothesis $hle$ asserts the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base changes of the full level-$M'$ modular function field and of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ for $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ (the kernel of `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`). $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa,M')$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the special-fibre field with kernel the maximal ideal, compatibility with $A$ under constants, a degree-preserving map on places, and the divisor-transport clause. The hypothesis $hR_0$ pins $R_0$ down on Laurent series with coefficients in $A$: for $y \in \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is an element of $W$, i.e. a supersingular place.
--
--   **Constant field.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$. Writing $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ (formally, `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`), the hypotheses require $A_0$ to be a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ ($hdvr$, $hunif$), henselian ($hhens$), with algebraically closed residue field ($hres$), and ($h\kappa$) every $a \in A$ to be congruent to some element of $k_0 \cap A$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime.** $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \neq q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Base clauses.** $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $k_0 \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b = \bot$, $A_b$ a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those of $A$, and $\varpi_b \neq 0$ a generator of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **Tameness and roots of unity.** $(\ell_g-1)/2$ is a unit of $A_0$ ($htame$), and $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity.
--
--   **Level data.** $H_1$ is the intersection of $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$; $K_\ell$ is the $k_0$-base change $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0\,(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,H_1)$, an intermediate field of $k_0 \subset k_0((\mathsf q))$, equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure forming a scalar tower through $k_0$; $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ is the element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$, and $j_\ell \neq 0$. Also $\varpi_t' \in A_0$ is an element mapping to $\varpi_t$ in $k_0$.
--
--   **The chart point.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of the finite-$j$ chart algebra $C := \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$, the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$; $h\varpi y$ requires $\pi_0 \in y$, and $hss$ requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_\ell)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$.
--
--   **Lying over $s$ ($hover$).** For every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb Q$ whose $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that $g$ has nonnegative order at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which $j$ has nonnegative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$: whenever the coefficientwise image of $g$ lies in $K_\ell$ and in $C$, and $c \in k_0 \cap A$ has residue in $\kappa$ equal to $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of $g$ and the image of $c$ lies in $y$.
--
--   **Orbit clause ($hOrbit$).** For every maximal ideal $y'$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same lying-over-$s$ condition, there are $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and a $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` — that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ (the constant series of $p_g$ nonzero), every $x \in K_\ell$ representing $p_f/p_g$, and every embedding $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, one has $\iota(\tau x) \cdot (g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})^\wedge = (f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})^\wedge$ on $q$-expansions — such that $\tau$ preserves $C$ and, for $f \in C$, $f \in y \iff \tau f \in y'$.
--
--   **The rigid chart ($Bt$, $Wt$, $hS1$).** $Bt$ is an $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ and $Wt$ a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with $Bt \subseteq Wt$. The hypothesis $hS1$ (thirteen clauses, summarised here) requires: $C \le Bt$; $K_\ell$ is the fraction field of $Bt$; $Bt$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$; $Bt/(\pi_0)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $Wt \cap k_0 = A_0$; the maximal ideal of $Wt$ is generated by $\pi_0$; $Wt$ is a discrete valuation ring; $Wt$ is centred at $y$ (for $b \in C$, $b \in y$ iff $b$ lies in the maximal ideal of $Wt$); $Wt$ is the localisation of $Bt$ at that maximal ideal; a $\rho$-block asserting, for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on the residue field $\lambda$ of $A_0$, the existence of a surjection $\rho : Bt \to \mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing}\,q\,\lambda = \lambda[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1)$ with kernel the centre of $Wt$, compatible with $A_0 \to \lambda$, and equivariant: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $Wt$ there is a scalar $c \in (\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2)^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ (the kernel of $(g,c) \mapsto \det g \cdot c^{q+1}$) such that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathrm{hAction}(\cdot)\circ\rho$ on $Bt$, with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$, together with the linked-scalars clause that the same $c$ is realised by some $\gamma' \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphism $\tau'$ at $\gamma'^{-1}$ preserving $Wt$ through the pair $(1,c) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$; stability of $Bt$ under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; transitivity on the primes of $Bt$ containing $\pi_0$ by level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; and the divisibility clause that $b \in Bt$ lying in the centre of $Wt$ after every such level automorphism is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   **Rotation data ($n$, $\gamma_0$, $\tau_0$, $m$, $\zeta_c$, $ends$, $hR7$).** $n \ge 1$ divides $q+1$; $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau_0$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ preserving $Wt$; $m \ge 1$ satisfies $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t' \cdot(\text{unit})$ in $A_0$; $\zeta_c$ lies in the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ with $\zeta_c^n = 1$ and $\zeta_c^k - 1$ a unit for $0 < k < n$; $ends$ is a finite set of subrings of $K_\ell$. The hypothesis $hR7$ (summarised here) requires: $\tau_0$ acts on $Bt$ with exact order $n$; every level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $Wt$ agrees on $Bt$ with a power $\tau_0^k$, $k < n$; $ends$ has exactly $q+1$ elements, is permuted by the level automorphisms at $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $Wt$, transitively so, and each member is stabilised by $\tau_0$; distinct members are separated by an element that is a nonunit in one and a unit in the other; and for each $O \in ends$: $O \subseteq Wt$, $O$ is local and noetherian, contains $C$, satisfies $O \cap k_0 = A_0$, no element of $O$ is a unit distance from all constants, and the adic completion of $O$ is isomorphic to the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,\widehat{A_0}\,(\pi_0^m) = \widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^m)$ over the constants, with elements $c_x, c_y \in O$ satisfying $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m \cdot(\text{unit})$ and mapping to unit multiples of $U$ and of $V$, $c_y$ in the centre of $Wt$ and $c_x$ outside it, $\tau_0$ corresponding to an automorphism $\theta_0$ of the crossing model with $\theta_0(U) \equiv \zeta_c U$ and $\theta_0(V) \equiv \zeta_c' V$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal ($\zeta_c\zeta_c' = 1$), together with the branch clauses: existence of a discrete valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ containing $O$ and $C$ with $W_x \cap k_0 = A_0$, uniformiser $\pi_0$, a transcendence-type clause for an element $t \in W_x$, $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its centre, and its centre on $C$ contained in but different from $y$; and existence of a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_x \subseteq Bt \cap O$, stable under the level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, consisting of functions regular where $j_\ell$ is, with $O$ its localisation. A final clause of $hR7$ states that every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ with $V \cap k_0 = A_0$, containing $C$ and centred at $y$ on $C$, either contains $Bt$ or dominates one of the members of $ends$.
--
--   **Compatibility ($hR5d$).** For $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$: if $\tau$ preserves $y$ on $C$, then $\tau$ preserves $Wt$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all these hypotheses,
--   $$n = \mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s,$$
--   that is, $n$ equals the natural-number quotient of $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\,q\,(s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M'))$ by $\mathrm{placeRamificationJ}\,M'\,s = (s.\mathrm{ord}(\mathrm{jGeomGen} - s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})))^+$; since $q = 2$, the numerator is $12$ if the $j$-value of $s$ is $0$ and $1$ otherwise. The equality is stated without a factor $2$, in contrast with the corresponding identity for $q \ge 5$.
--
--   This is the width identity of the rigid-chart analysis of the supersingular points: it identifies the order $n$ of the rotation $\tau_0$ acting on the rigid chart at a supersingular point of the integral model of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $A_0$ with the width $\mathrm{placeWidthChar}$ of the supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ modular function field below it, in the $q = 2$ frame with a guard prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$. It feeds the construction of semistable supersingular charts, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
